.TH "GENERIC CONTAINER MACROS AND TYPE DEFINITIONS." "3" "" "libiter 2.0.1" "libiter manual"
.SH NAME
Generic container macros and type definitions. \- API reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <iter/types.h>\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_container(T_CNTR, T_ITEM)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_item_type(T_CNTR, CNTR)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_item_ptr(T_CNTR, CNTR)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_item_dptr(T_CNTR, CNTR)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_item_size(T_CNTR, CNTR)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_check_item(T_CNTR, CNTR, ITEM)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_check_item_d(T_CNTR, CNTR, ITEM)\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB#define generic_check_container(T_CNTR, CNTR)\fR
.fi
.SH REFERENCE
.SS generic_container
.PP
Declares a type generic container with given types
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Type of the container.
.IP \(bu 2
T_ITEM \- Type of the item.
.SS generic_item_type
.PP
Extracts the item type of the given container.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.SS generic_item_ptr
.PP
Extracts the item type with a pointer of the given container.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.SS generic_item_dptr
.PP
Extracts the item type with a double pointer of the given container.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.SS generic_item_size
.PP
Extracts the item type with a pointer of the given container.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.SS generic_check_item
.PP
Check if given item's type matches container's subtype.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.IP \(bu 2
ITEM \- Pointer to the given item.
.SS generic_check_item_d
.PP
Check if given double\-pointer item's type matches container's subtype.
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.IP \(bu 2
ITEM \- Pointer to the given item.
.SS generic_check_container
.PP
Check if given container is of the given type (not subtype).
.PP
Parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
T_CNTR \- Explicit type of the container, or .
.IP \(bu 2
CNTR \- Pointer to the actual container.
.SH ERROR HANDLING
Errors are reported with the codes of
.B enum libiter_error
from
.IR <iter/types.h> .
.B ITER_OK
(0) means success; every other code is a negative value, such as
.B ITER_EINVAL
or
.BR ITER_ENOMEM .
.PP
Functions that document
.B Returns
report the error by returning its code.
.PP
Functions that document
.B Exceptions
(or
.BR Throws )
emit the error through the
.I <pf_exception.h>
interface.
Wrap the call so the exception can be caught with
.BR libiter_catch ()
(see
.BR global (3)),
which returns
.B NULL
on the first call and the emitted exception afterwards.
Functions that return a pointer return
.B NULL
when an exception was emitted, and functions that return an integer return the
error code.
The exception stack is thread local.
